# API Contract Conventions

The authoritative source is `Docs/integration/APIContract.md`. These are the most frequently referenced rules.

## Request/Response Shape

- Base path: `/api/v1`
- JSON `camelCase` field naming
- Success envelope: `{ data, page?, meta: { requestId } }`
- Error envelope: `{ error: { code, message, fieldErrors?, requestId } }`
- Time format: ISO 8601 with timezone (`2026-09-01T08:30:00+08:00`)
- Duration: integer **minutes** only, never hours, never decimal
- Amounts: integer **centi-coins** (7550 = 75.5 coins), never decimal

## Authentication

- `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax` cookies (Spring Session JDBC)
- CSRF token required on mutations (cookie double-submit)
- Session timeouts: ~8h staff / ~12h student (configurable)

## Error Codes

| HTTP | Code | Meaning |
|------|------|---------|
| 400 | `INVALID_REQUEST` | Malformed request |
| 401 | `AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED` | Not logged in / session expired |
| 403 | `FORBIDDEN` | No permission (must not reveal if resource exists) |
| 404 | `RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND` | Not found or not visible to caller |
| 409 | `STATE_CONFLICT` | Wrong state, duplicate op, or version conflict |
| 422 | `VALIDATION_FAILED` | Field or business validation |
| 429 | `RATE_LIMITED` | Throttled |

## Pagination & Filtering

- `page[number]`, `page[size]` (server max 100)
- `sort=field` / `sort=-field` (desc)
- `filter[field]=value`
- `search=text` for free-text
- Stable ordering with `id` tiebreaker

## Concurrency Control

- `@Version` column on editable entities
- Client sends version on updates; `409` if stale
- `Idempotency-Key` header on: record submission, review decisions, account adjustments, proposal approval, import commit
- Duplicate key → replay stored response, never double-credit

## Localization

- `Accept-Language` on every request (`zh-CN` or `en`)
- Dictionary/category names come from server, localized
- Status values are enum codes — frontend labels them
- Unknown enum values render as the raw code, never blank
